## Why the Technician Matters at a Wedding

Most of our packages don't include a technician as standard; the Wedding Pack does, alongside only the MICE Pack built for corporate conferences. At a wedding, that matters more than at almost any other event: vows and speeches happen once, live, in front of everyone who matters to you. A technician on site catches a microphone feedback loop or a dropped connection before it becomes the thing people remember, and adjusts sound levels as the day moves from ceremony to speeches to dancing.

## What We Provide, and What We Don't

We provide sound, lighting and microphones for the ceremony and reception, plus the technician to run it. We do not provide a projector, screen or LED display: the Wedding Pack has none, since a wedding rarely needs one. We also do not provide furniture, decor, dancefloor accessories, or photography and videography. If a page or vendor implies otherwise, ask them to itemize it: AV equipment and those other trades are typically separate services.

